    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="20.1">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:LeisWl">Leis Wl</ref> 20.1</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" corresp="#wit-hk"><pb n="506–507" ed="#liebermann"/>De relief a barun: IIII chevals, les II enfrenez e enseelez, e II haubercs e II haumes e II escuz e II espees<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="cc" target="#LeisWl_20-1.lnote.oe.cc"/> e II lances. E les autres II chevals: un chaceur e un palefrei a freins e a chevestres.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" corresp="#wit-i"><ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#LeisWl_20-1.lnote.oe.9"/><pb n="506–507" ed="#liebermann"/>De relief<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#LeisWl_20-1.lnote.oe.10"/> a barun: IIII chivalz, . . . .<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="b" target="#LeisWl_20-1.lnote.oe.b"/> enselez<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#LeisWl_20-1.lnote.oe.11"/> e enfrenez<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="12" target="#LeisWl_20-1.lnote.oe.12"/>, e II halberz<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="13" target="#LeisWl_20-1.lnote.oe.13"/> e II haumes<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#LeisWl_20-1.lnote.oe.5"/> e II escuz<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="14" target="#LeisWl_20-1.lnote.oe.14"/> e II launces e II espés. E les altres II . . .<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="c" target="#LeisWl_20-1.lnote.oe.c"/>: un chaceur e un palafrei<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="15" target="#LeisWl_20-1.lnote.oe.15"/> a freins<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#LeisWl_20-1.lnote.oe.7"/> e a chevestres.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" corresp="#wit-l"><pb n="506–507" ed="#liebermann"/>Releuium baronis: IIII equi, ex quibus duo sellati erunt et frenati, et cum eis lorice due, scuta II, galee II, lancee II, gladii II. Reliquorum duorum equorum alter erit palefridus, alter chaçur<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#LeisWl_20-1.lnote.oe.2"/> cum frenis et chamis<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="b" target="#LeisWl_20-1.lnote.oe.b-2"/>.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="xno" source="#robertson" n="20.1" corresp="#wit-hk"><pb n="262" ed="#robertson"/>De relief a barun: IIII chevals, les II enfrenez e enseelez, e II haubercs e II haumes e II escuz e II espees e II lances. E les autres II chevals: un chaceur e un palefrei a freins e a chevestres.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="506–507" ed="#liebermann"/>20, 1. An Heergeräthe für einen Baron<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="b" target="#LeisWl_20-1.lnote.de1.b"/>: 4 Pferde, davon 2 gezäumt und gesattelt, und 2 Panzerhemden und 2 Helme und 2 Schilde und 2 Schwerter und 2 Lanzen. Und die anderen beiden Pferde: 1 Jagdpferd und 1 Zelter mit Zäumen und mit Halftern.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">20, 1. As heriot for a baron: 4 horses, of them 2 bridled and saddled, and 2 coats of mail and 2 helmets and 2 shields and 2 swords and 2 lances. And the other two horses: 1 hunting horse and 1 palfrey with bridles and with halters.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-hk"><pb n="263" ed="#robertson"/>The heriot of a baron is 4 horses—2 bridled and saddled—2 coats of mail, 2 helmets, 2 shields, 2 swords and 2 lances. And of the other two horses, 1 shall be a hunter and 1 a riding horse with bridles and halters.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="507"><ref target="clause:IICn_71-1">II Cn 71.1</ref></note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">ebd. 71, 1</note>
        <note type="editorial">Added October 2026 from Robertson pp. 262–263 (text and translation); Liebermann’s text and German translation added from Gesetze I p. 506–507, October 2026 (two independent readings of the page images)</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_20-1.lnote.oe.cc" n="cc" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">506</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">so, gegen</hi> IL, <hi rend="italic">ordnet Cnut</hi> swurd <hi rend="italic">vor</hi> spera</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">so; against IL, Cnut puts swurd before spera</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_20-1.lnote.oe.b" n="b" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">506</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">ergänze</hi> les II <hi rend="italic">aus HkL</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">supply les II from HkL</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_20-1.lnote.oe.c" n="c" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">506</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">ergänze</hi> chivals <hi rend="italic">laut HkL</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">supply chivals according to HkL</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_20-1.lnote.oe.5" n="5" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">506</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">hammes <hi rend="italic">Io</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">hammes <hi rend="italic">Io</hi></seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_20-1.lnote.oe.7" n="7" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">506</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">frenis <hi rend="italic">Io</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">frenis <hi rend="italic">Io</hi></seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_20-1.lnote.oe.9" n="9" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">506</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">XXIII. <hi rend="italic">Im</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">XXIII. <hi rend="italic">Im</hi></seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_20-1.lnote.oe.10" n="10" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">506</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">releif <hi rend="italic">Io</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">releif <hi rend="italic">Io</hi></seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_20-1.lnote.oe.11" n="11" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">506</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-les <hi rend="italic">Io</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-les <hi rend="italic">Io</hi></seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_20-1.lnote.oe.12" n="12" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">506</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-nes <hi rend="italic">Io</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-nes <hi rend="italic">Io</hi></seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_20-1.lnote.oe.13" n="13" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">506</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-ers <hi rend="italic">Io</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-ers <hi rend="italic">Io</hi></seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_20-1.lnote.oe.14" n="14" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">506</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">escus <hi rend="italic">Io</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">escus <hi rend="italic">Io</hi></seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_20-1.lnote.oe.15" n="15" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">506</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">palef. <hi rend="italic">Io</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">palef. <hi rend="italic">Io</hi></seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_20-1.lnote.oe.b-2" n="b" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">507</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">in der Griech. Bibel</hi> χάμος</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">in the Greek Bible χάμος</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_20-1.lnote.oe.2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">507</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">nicht mit Edd.</hi> chascur</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">not chascur, as edd.</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="translationFootnote" xml:id="LeisWl_20-1.lnote.de1.b" n="b" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">507</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">dem Könige nächsten Thegn; <hi rend="italic">Cnut</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">thegn nearest to the king; Cnut</seg></note>
      </div>
